---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Hero from '../components/Hero.astro';

const pageTitle = 'Privacy & Cookie Policy | Ruth Lara Reyes';
const pageDescription = 'EU GDPR Privacy and Cookie Policy for Ruth Lara Reyes (Florence, Italy).';
---

<BaseLayout title={pageTitle} description={pageDescription}>
	<div class="stack gap-15">
		<div class="wrapper">
			<Hero
				title="Privacy & Cookie Policy"
				tagline="Information pursuant to Articles 13 and 14 of Regulation (EU) 2016/679 (GDPR). Last updated: November 2026."
				align="start"
			/>
		</div>

		<main class="wrapper content stack gap-8">
			<section class="stack gap-3">
				<h2>1. Data Controller</h2>
				<p>
					The Data Controller is <strong>Ruth Lara Reyes</strong>, based in Florence (FI), Italy.<br />
					<strong>Contact Email:</strong> <a href="mailto:YOUR-EMAIL@DOMAIN.COM">YOUR-EMAIL@DOMAIN.COM</a>
				</p>
			</section>

			<section class="stack gap-3">
				<h2>2. Types of Data Processed, Purpose &amp; Legal Basis</h2>
				<ul>
					<li>
						<strong>Browsing &amp; Technical Security Logs:</strong> When you visit this website, our
						hosting infrastructure provider (<strong>Cloudflare, Inc.</strong>) automatically processes
						technical connection data (such as IP address, browser type, and timestamp) strictly to
						deliver pages securely and protect against malicious traffic. <em>Legal basis:</em>
						Legitimate interest in website security and operation (Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR).
					</li>
					<li>
						<strong>Direct Inquiries &amp; Appointment Bookings:</strong> If you contact me via email
						or schedule a consultation through my external <strong>Google Calendar</strong> booking page,
						I process your name, email address, and message details solely to respond to your inquiry
						or conduct the requested call. <em>Legal basis:</em> Pre-contractual measures taken at your
						request (Art. 6(1)(b) GDPR).
					</li>
				</ul>
			</section>

			<section class="stack gap-3">
				<h2>3. Third-Party Service Providers &amp; International Transfers</h2>
				<p>
					Data may be processed by trusted technical providers acting as Data Processors under GDPR
					Data Processing Agreements: <strong>Cloudflare</strong> (website hosting and CDN) and
					<strong>Google Ireland Limited</strong> (email and appointment scheduling). Where data is
					processed outside the European Economic Area (EEA), transfers are safeguarded by the EU–U.S.
					Data Privacy Framework or European Commission Standard Contractual Clauses (SCCs).
				</p>
			</section>

			<section class="stack gap-3">
				<h2>4. Data Retention</h2>
				<p>
					Technical security logs are retained only for the brief period necessary for security
					monitoring. Inquiry and booking data are retained only as long as needed to handle your
					request or fulfill applicable legal and tax obligations.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section class="stack gap-3">
				<h2>5. Cookie &amp; Local Storage Notice</h2>
				<p>
					This website does <strong>not</strong> use advertising, profiling, or third-party tracking
					cookies. It uses only strictly necessary technical browser storage (such as remembering your
					light/dark theme preference), which does not require prior consent under EU ePrivacy rules
					and the Italian Data Protection Authority (Garante Privacy) guidelines.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section class="stack gap-3">
				<h2>6. Your Rights Under the GDPR</h2>
				<p>
					Under Articles 15–22 of the GDPR, you have the right to request access to, rectification of,
					or erasure of your personal data, as well as restriction of processing, data portability,
					and objection. You may exercise these rights at any time by writing to
					<a href="mailto:iteltur@gmail.com">iteltur@gmail.com</a>. You also have the right to
					lodge a complaint with the Italian Supervisory Authority (<strong>Garante per la protezione dei dati personali</strong>,
					<a href="https://garanteprivacy.it" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">www.garanteprivacy.it</a>)
					or your local EU data protection authority.
				</p>
			</section>
		</main>
	</div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
	.content {
		max-width: 68ch;
		color: var(--gray-200);
		line-height: 1.7;
	}

	.content h2 {
		font-size: var(--text-xl);
		color: var(--gray-0);
	}

	.content ul {
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		gap: 0.75rem;
		padding-left: 1.25rem;
	}

	.content a {
		color: var(--accent-regular);
		text-decoration: underline;
	}
</style>

